        <h2>Executive Summary</h2>

        <p>This protocol offers a ΔHV-based coherence structure for gender emergence when field distortions—caused by trauma, neglect, symbolic inversion, or developmental rupture—have interfered with natural identity formation. Rather than determining 'authenticity' of gender identity, this protocol maps coherence patterns to distinguish:</p>

        <ul class="protocol-list">
            <li>Authentic emergence requiring affirmation</li>
            <li>Archetypal exploration requiring containment</li>
            <li>Trauma-driven fixation requiring processing</li>
            <li>Natural integration requiring support</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Core Premise</h3>

        <p>Gender is not merely a social role or identity label. It is an emergent harmonic pattern between self and other, shaped by tone, resonance, reflection, containment, and witnessing. Gender coherence is not determined by performance but by phase-stable feedback in relational fields.</p>

        <p><strong>Foundational Principle:</strong> High coherence across domains indicates integration in progress. Low/chaotic coherence indicates blocked emergence requiring different intervention. The ΔHV stability analysis demonstrates that approximately 25-35% of parameter space naturally flows toward sustained high-coherence attractors, while low-coherence states remain unstable and require intervention to escape chaotic cycling.</p>

        <div class="warning-box">
            <h4>Critical Distinction</h4>
            <p>A queer response to trauma does not define one's core essence—it reflects the body's adaptation to survive relational incoherence.</p>
        </div>
    </section>

